30. Framework Statement

C.A.N.O.N.™ is an author-developed constitutional-grade governance architecture designed to examine how institutions can preserve legitimacy, accountability, resilience, adaptability, and continuity under conditions of technological disruption, systemic crisis, geopolitical complexity, and long-horizon uncertainty.

Its principal contribution is the integration of legitimacy analysis, constitutional stress testing, executive-power review, ethical safeguards, crisis governance, intergenerational responsibility, AI governance, global compatibility, and institutional self-correction within a unified governance architecture.

The framework is intended to support serious research, structured institutional analysis, scenario testing, policy discussion, and potential implementation subject to independent validation, jurisdiction-specific requirements, and applicable law.

